//? Title: Karger's contraction: preserve a cut by avoiding its edges
//? Subtitle: Actual sampled edges, component snapshots and complete trial partitions
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Random contraction samples crossing edges until two components remain, then
counts the original edges between them. We inspect actual producing
contractions, retain the original triangle-plus-bridge experiment, and
distinguish a sampled candidate from a certified minimum. Loops, parallel edges
and disconnected inputs are explicit. Native histories own component labels and
every trial partition; finite seed censuses are separated from ideal-random
success bounds.
)

\toc

> Look at one actual merge

Use a triangle with a bridge to vertex3. A contraction joins the components of
one sampled original edge. Labels in the following table are the minimum
original vertex in each actual component after the merge, not internal
union-find roots. The diagram reads the first actual selected edge and the
resulting component count; no replay reconstructs the decision.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/karger_merge.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t, std::size_t>> edges = {{0, 1},
                                                                    {1, 2},
                                                                    {2, 0},
                                                                    {2, 3}};
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::karger_trace(4, edges, 1, 7);
    std::print("| contraction | groups before | selected original edge | crossing choices | chosen rank | " "groups after |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.steps.size(); ++i) {
        const auto &s = t.steps[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, s.groups_before,
                   s.edge_index, s.crossing_count, s.chosen_rank, s.groups_after);
    }
    std::print("\n| contraction | vertex | actual component label |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.steps.size(); ++i)
        for (std::size_t v = 0; v < 4; ++v)
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", i, v, t.steps[i].labels[v]);
    const auto &s = t.steps.front();
    const auto[u, v] = edges[s.edge_index];
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("before", {0, 0}, std::format("{} components", s.groups_before)).node("edge", {5, 0}, std::format("Actual edge {}\n{} -- {}", s.edge_index, u, v)).node("after", {10, 0}, std::format("{} components", s.groups_after)).edge("before", "edge").edge("edge", "after").save_svg("build/karger_merge.svg");
}
```
