> Derive the survival bound under ideal randomness

Fix a minimum cut of positive size k in a connected undirected multigraph. With
r supervertices, each has degree at least k, so there are at least rk/2 crossing
edges, counting multiplicity. A uniformly selected crossing edge hits the fixed
cut with probability at most 2/r. Thus

$$
\Pr(\text{fixed cut survives})\geq\prod_{r=n}^{3}(1-2/r)=\frac{2}{n(n-1)}.
$$
\alttext(The product of conditional cut-survival probabilities telescopes to two divided by n times n minus one.)

For B independent ideal trials the failure probability is at most (1−2/(n(n−1)))
to the power B. This is a model guarantee, not an observed confidence level for
one deterministic pseudorandom seed. A disconnected graph instead has a zero
cut, handled directly by the component partition when no crossing edges remain.

The native kernel keeps parallel-edge multiplicity, discards loops from
contraction candidates, and rebuilds the input-ordered crossing list after each
merge. It uses rejection before modulo reduction to remove finite-word modulo
bias. For bound b, reject words below (2^64 mod b), then reduce an accepted word
modulo b. This differs from the former raw-modulo implementation only when a
rejection occurs; actual accepted words and draw counts are recorded.

> Retain the original bridge experiment

The original call uses four vertices, edges (0,1),(1,2),(2,0),(2,3), one hundred
trials and seed7. The table shows the actual retained candidate and its
partition. Because this particular graph is connected and has a bridge, a
returned crossing count of one is also a deterministic optimality certificate.
That reasoning does not generalize to an arbitrary positive returned cut.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/karger_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t, std::size_t>> edges = {{0, 1},
                                                                    {1, 2},
                                                                    {2, 0},
                                                                    {2, 3}};
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::karger_trace(4, edges, 100, 7);
    std::print("| cut size | completed trials | actual contractions | candidate edge checks | cut edge " "checks | random draws |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | " "{} | {} |\n",
               t.result.cut_size, t.work.trials, t.work.contractions,
               t.work.candidate_edge_checks, t.work.cut_edge_checks,
               t.work.random_draws);
    std::print("\n| vertex | actual retained side |\n| ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t v = 0; v < 4; ++v)
        std::print("| {} | {} |\n", v,
                   std::find(t.result.side_a.begin(), t.result.side_a.end(), v) !=
                   t.result.side_a.end() ? "A" : "B");
    if (t.result.cut_size != 1)
        throw std::runtime_error("bridge minimum");
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;
    style.width = 1.3;
    style.circle = true;
    const dm::graphics::DiagramPoint positions[] = {{0, 0}, {6, 0}, {3, 5},
                                                    {9, 5}};
    for (std::size_t v = 0; v < 4; ++v)
        d.node(std::to_string(v), positions[v], std::to_string(v), style);
    for (auto[u, v] : edges) {
        const bool a =
            std::find(t.result.side_a.begin(), t.result.side_a.end(), u) !=
            t.result.side_a.end(), b =
            std::find(t.result.side_a.begin(), t.result.side_a.end(), v) !=
            t.result.side_a.end();
        dm::graphics::DiagramStroke stroke;
        stroke.color =
            a != b ? dm::graphics::RGB{220, 38, 38}
            : dm::graphics::RGB{100, 116, 139};
        stroke.width = a != b ? 4 : 2;
        d.link(std::to_string(u), std::to_string(v), a != b ? "cut" : "", stroke);
    }
    d.save_svg("build/karger_original.svg");
}
```
