> A finite seed census is evidence, not a confidence certificate

The following complete census uses seeds0 through31 for each trial budget on the
same four-vertex graph. The exact minimum is one by the bridge argument.
Observed failure fraction is compared with the ideal independent-trial upper
bound, which need not bound every finite deterministic seed census. The graph
and all budgets are controlled inputs, so no external dataset is needed.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/karger_profile.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t, std::size_t>> edges = {{0, 1},
                                                                    {1, 2},
                                                                    {2, 0},
                                                                    {2, 3}};
    std::vector<double> x, observed, bound;
    std::print("| trial budget | complete seeds | failures to find one | observed fraction | ideal-model " "failure bound |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t budget = 1; budget <= 128; budget *= 2) {
        std::size_t failures = 0;
        for (std::uint64_t seed = 0; seed < 32; ++seed)
            failures +=
                dm::algorithms::karger_min_cut(4, edges, budget, seed).cut_size !=
                1;
        const double fraction =
            failures / 32., upper = std::pow(1. - 2. / (4. * 3.), budget);
        std::print("| {} | 32 | {} | {:.9f} | {:.12e} |\n", budget, failures,
                   fraction, upper);
        x.push_back(std::log2(budget));
        observed.push_back(fraction);
        bound.push_back(upper);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, observed, "census", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, observed, "",
                                                           {37, 99, 235}, 4).line(x, bound, "ideal bound", {220, 38, 38}, 2).title("Finite seeded outcomes versus an ideal-model bound").x_label("log2(actual trial budget)").y_label("failure fraction or bound").y_limits(-.04, 1.05).save_svg("build/karger_profile.svg");
}
```
